54), which protects the c4 pawn, which was hanging."],"better":"25.b3 protects the c4 pawn. After 25…Rd3 26.fxe4 fxe4 27.Ng2 Rff3 28.Rxe4 Rxb3 29.Nf4 Rxa3 30.Nd5+, White is a pawn down (−1.54)."},{"ply":50,"name":"25…e3","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"25…e3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Creates a passed pawn on e3: no enemy pawn can stop it any more.","Moving away uncovers the rook on d4, which now hits the knight on h4.","The next best move, 25…Re8, would drop Black's winning chances from 76% to 66% (−1.81).","25…e3 stops fxe4.","White was threatening fxe4, winning a pawn. e3 takes care of it.","White answers 26.f4, taking e5 away from the knight on c6."]},{"ply":60,"name":"30…b6","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"30…b6! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Protects the c5 pawn, which was hanging.","Takes c5 away from the rook on c1.","The next best move, 30…Kb6, would drop Black's winning chances from 74% to 64% (−1.51).","30…b6 wins a pawn, picking it up with 31…Rxf3.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 31…Rxf3.","White answers 31.Red1."]},{"ply":64,"name":"32…Rg8+","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"32…Rg8+ lets the win slip: 32…Nd3 kept Black winning. Black's winning chances go from 75% to 61%.","points":["White answers 33.Kh1: the king steps out of check to h1.","Better was 32…Nd3 (−2.96): the knight forks the rook and the pawn: both can't be saved at once."],"better":"32…Nd3 wins a pawn, picking it up with 33…Nxf4, and gets the knight out of the way of fxe5. After 33.Rb1 Nxf4 34.Rf3 Kc6 35.Rbf1 Re8, Black comes out a pawn up (−2.96)."},{"ply":87,"name":"44.Kg4","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"44.Kg4 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 34% to 15%.","points":["Black answers 44…Nxf5, which takes the pawn on f5.","After Nxf5, Black wins 1 point of material within 2 moves.","Better was 44.Nh4 (−1.81): shores up the f5 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (3 against 1)."],"better":"44.Nh4 stops …Ne4+. Engine line: 44…Rf8 45.Kh2 Re4 46.Ng2 Rf7 47.Kg3 (−1.81)."},{"ply":88,"name":"44…Nxf5","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"44…Nxf5!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the knight on f5 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: White's best reply is 45.Kg5 Rg6+ 46.Kf4 Rd5 instead (the engine rates it −4.53).","Takes the pawn on f5.","44…Nxf5 wins a pawn.","Takes the f5 pawn and wins a pawn once the captures settle.","White answers 45.Kg5, attacking the rook on f6, which is undefended."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"44…Nxf5!! offers the knight on f5. Taking it gives Black the material back and more."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"44…Nxf5 puts the knight on f5 where it can be taken by the rook on f2. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"If White takes the knight","text":"45.Rxf5 is met by 45…Rg6+, and the rook on f6 gets away. Then 46…Rxf5+ gives check, and 47…Rxg2 takes the knight on g2. Black ends up a pawn ahead: Black is winning (−5.53)."},{"title":"White's best try","text":"White's best is to leave the knight alone and play 45.Kg5. Black answers 45…Rg6+, and the rook on f6 gets away. Then 47…Nxe3 takes the knight on e3, and 48…Re6+ gives check. Black ends up a pawn ahead: Black is winning (−4.53)."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 44…Rf8, is clearly weaker (−2.48 against −4.53). White answers 45.f6, pushing the passed pawn to f6. Black would still be clearly better, but far less than after 44…Nxf5."}]}],"opening":{"name":"English Opening: Anglo-Indian Defense, Queen's Knight Variation","eco":"A16","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 7.Bxd2: 13 moves in all, 7 by White and 6 by Black.","Theory runs out after 7.Bxd2: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}